From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: send routed frames from pages

With mac80211's TXQs off, a frame the switch routed to an AP interface in
Ethernet encapsulation needs nothing from mac80211. Take it as the page the
switch driver received it in, map it without a cache sync and queue it on
the TCL ring; the completion counts it for its station and returns the page
to its pool. Frames to unauthorized, TKIP or 4-address stations, multicast
and non-IP frames take the normal path.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
